Tally 1.0 for RISC OS
=====================

An example program from riscos-crossdev, built with CMake: it lists the
words used most often in a text file, which may be gzipped.

Double-click !Tally to count the words in this file. After that, from
the command line (F12):

  *Tally <file> [<how many>]

Requirements: RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 machine with VFP (a Raspberry Pi 2
or later, or a Cortex-A8/A9 board); SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later and
ARMEABISupport, both from PackMan.

